      "jcr:created": "Fri Sep 25 2026 15:45:52 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<h2><span class=\"futura-bold\">Learn how proactive fecal management can help support skin integrity, infection prevention and nursing workflow.</span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">In a fast-moving care environment, fecal management can shift from routine to urgent before a team has time to assess the situation. What starts at the bedside can quickly influence skin integrity, contamination risk, nursing workload and the care environment around the patient. For bedside nurses and nursing leaders, it’s a reminder that fecal incontinence deserves attention and requires practical strategies to support care.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">In this on-demand webinar, Anna Daigle, MBA-HCM, BSN, RN, CNRN takes a closer look at the often-overlooked role fecal management plays in patient safety, infection prevention and workflow. The session is designed for the clinicians who see these challenges firsthand and the leaders working to standardize care, support staff and protect patient outcomes.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">If your unit is already feeling the pressure of competing priorities, rising expectations and complex patient needs, this is one conversation you won’t want to miss. Fill out the form below to access the full webinar recording and gain insights that can help your team see fecal management with new clarity, urgency and purpose.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Sep 25 2026 15:46:45 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true"
    },
